  <section id="faq">
    <h2>What else do people ask about finding where AI helps?</h2>

    <h3>How do I know if my business is ready for AI?</h3>
    <p>If your people spend their days copying, chasing, checking and answering the same
       questions, there is usually something to find. Readiness also depends on whether the
       information those steps need is written down and reachable. Map one team's work and you
       will know quickly; the free call with us gives you an honest view too.</p>

    <h3>Where can AI help my business first?</h3>
    <p>In the team with the most hours spent on high-volume reading, writing, sorting and
       answering. That is found by timing and counting the steps, not by picking the most
       popular tool. Start with one or two steps where a mistake is cheap or a person checks the
       result.</p>

    <h3>What should not use AI?</h3>
    <p>Rare tasks, tasks with fixed rules that plain automation handles, and expert judgements
       where a mistake is costly. Steps sitting on a messy process should wait until the process
       is fixed. Saying no to AI for those steps saves money.</p>

    <h3>Is this an audit of our accounts or a certification?</h3>
    <p>No. Our assessment is an operational review of how work gets done and where AI can help.
       It is not a financial audit, an assurance report or a certification of any AI system.
       More answers are in <a href="/consulting/#questions">our assessment questions</a>.</p>

    <h3>Do you work outside Dubai?</h3>
    <p>Yes. We are based in Dubai and work on site with businesses across the Gulf: Abu Dhabi
       and the rest of the UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Kuwait, Bahrain and Oman. The timeline is
       agreed in writing before we start.</p>
  </section>
